Not to be confused with the [[Dragon]] body type. 

This category is for tuxemon and trainers that, in-game, are linked to dragons. 

== Species name ==

Tuxemon with the Dragon species name are:

* The [[Wrougon]] family
* The [[Chloragon]] family
* The [[Drokoro]] family

The [[Agnite]] family are "False Dragons". The [[Agnigon]] blurb explains that they evolved "from a different line of ancient reptiles".

== Blurbs ==
[[Sapragon]]'s blurb says: "In olden times, each element had a mighty dragon - but those creatures have diminished and are rare in these days".

Between them, [[Wrougon]] represent [[Metal]], [[Chloragon]] [[Wood]] and [[Drokoro]] [[Fire]]. 

A number of blurbs give details about dragon tuxemon. Many of them imply that dragons are dying out, or in decline.

* [[Chloragon]] hatch from [[Ancient Egg]]s, but "When the eggs run out, there will be no more CHLORAGON". [[Dragarbor]] plant themselves in a graveyard where their tails grow forever. 
* [[Ferricran]] used to be covered in adamantine scales, and had wings of mithril. These metals have been turned into relics, which [[Allagon]] fights to retrieve. 
* Each [[Wrougon]] is born with a bigger patch of rust than its parents' patch.
* [[Drokoro]] ate all of its kind, making it [[unique]].

== Trainers ==

[[Dragonrider]]s are found in the [[Dragon's Cave]], where they guard [[Drokoro]]. Despite the Agnite family being "False Dragons", they are found in Dragon's Cave.